<article class="env-lemma" id="07QG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07QG">Lemma <span data-tag="07QG">10.166.5</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $A$ be an algebra over $k$. Let $k = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits k_ i$ be a directed colimit of subfields. If $A$ is geometrically regular over each $k_ i$, then $A$ is geometrically regular over $k$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $k'/k$ be a finite purely inseparable field extension. We can get $k'$ by adjoining finitely many variables to $k$ and imposing finitely many polynomial relations. Hence we see that there exists an $i$ and a finite purely inseparable field extension $k_ i'/k_ i$ such that $k_ i = k \otimes _{k_ i} k_ i'$. Thus $A \otimes _ k k' = A \otimes _{k_ i} k_ i'$ and the lemma is clear. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>